<title>UK: UK's Clarke sees RPIX inflation at 3 pct in 1998.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke sees RPIX inflation at 3 pct in 1998.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Treasury said in its &quot;Red Book&quot; financial statement and budget report that underlying inflation (RPIX) would run at 3.0 percent year-on-year in 1996, and fall to 2.5 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>The government has a medium-term target of 2.5 percent for underlying inflation. In October, RPIX (retail prices excluding mortgage interest payments) jumped to 3.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>(See separate summary of key economic forecasts, which will be issued shortly)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
